# Database schema

## No automatic “updated” fields

Do **not** use database or ORM machinery that changes audit or timestamp columns without explicit application code.

**Forbidden:**

- Drizzle `.$onUpdate(...)` on any column
- Postgres `BEFORE UPDATE` triggers that set `updated_at` (or similar)
- Column definitions that imply “always refresh on write” without the handler passing the value

**Allowed:**

- `DEFAULT now()` (or equivalent) on **insert only** for `created_at` / initial `updated_at`
- Setting `updated_at`, `updated_by`, and related fields in the **same transaction** as the business update (repository/service layer)

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — ORM auto-updates updated_at
updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow().notNull().$onUpdate(() => new Date()),

// ✅ GOOD — schema only; app sets on update
updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at", { withTimezone: true, mode: "date" }).defaultNow().notNull(),
// In update path: .set({ ...fields, updatedAt: new Date(), updatedBy: actorId })
```

When adding tables, spread `metadataColumns` from `metadata.ts` and keep this rule in mind for any one-off timestamp columns too.